secure-terminal-sigreport(1) -- print received signals (a Terminate test target)
=================================================================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2026 - 2026 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS

`secure-terminal --` `secure-terminal-sigreport`

## DESCRIPTION

secure-terminal-sigreport traps every catchable signal, prints `received
SIG<NAME> (<num>)` when one arrives, and keeps running. It is a diagnostic
target for the Terminate button (and the `/terminate` command): run it as the
terminal's program, click Terminate, and watch the `SIGTERM` land, followed
about two seconds later by the uncatchable `SIGKILL` that ends the process --
confirming the whole SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL escalation reached the foreground
group.

`SIGKILL` and `SIGSTOP` cannot be caught (the kernel never delivers them to a
handler), so they are not trapped; a `SIGKILL` simply makes the process vanish.

## EXIT STATUS

Exits 0 on `SIGQUIT` (Ctrl-\\). Otherwise it runs until killed.

## SEE ALSO

`secure-terminal`(1)
